3
00:00:06,370 --> 00:00:08,130
If you're taking the National Postgraduate Entrance Examination for a 985/211 university,

4
00:00:08,130 --> 00:00:09,590
Of course, it definitely helps.

5
00:00:09,590 --> 00:00:11,150
Getting into a 985/211 university is definitely a plus.

6
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:12,860
But if it's not a 985/211, it's useless.

7
00:00:12,860 --> 00:00:15,660
If it's not a '92 university, you might as well just hire someone with a bachelor's degree.

8
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:18,730
Okay, so is it useful to pursue a part-time master's in Amorphous metal after you've started working?

9
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:20,530
For a part-time master's, like the 'Fei Quan' one, you don't even need to bother taking the exam.

10
00:00:20,530 --> 00:00:21,329
It's a real waste of time.

11
00:00:21,329 --> 00:00:24,000
Well, unless... I mean, you can't just say it's a waste of time.

12
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,239
If you want to improve yourself, then sure, that's a different story.

13
00:00:25,239 --> 00:00:26,760
But if your only goal is to get a job,

14
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:29,080
or especially for integrated/embedded systems, it's not that significant.

15
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:31,300
So, what do employers value most when hiring recent graduates?

16
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,440
One thing is their verbal communication skills.

17
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:36,659
That's something I'd also pay attention to.

18
00:00:36,659 --> 00:00:40,979
Then, what kind of competitions they've participated in during their time at school.

19
00:00:40,979 --> 00:00:42,900
That's the kind of thing that would pique my interest.

20
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:48,900
And also, has he written anything on his own?

21
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:49,780
Yeah, things like having written a blog, that would also catch my eye.

22
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:51,220
Sometimes, that piques my interest as well.

23
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:52,659
Basically, in any area, as long as it's tech-related,

24
00:00:52,659 --> 00:00:53,680
I'll be interested in it.

25
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:55,560
I'm not limited to just one thing.

26
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:59,440
Well, as a fresh graduate, you'll always have your own unique strengths to showcase.

27
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:02,080
You can't just expect it to stay in one place.

28
00:01:02,610 --> 00:01:04,090
Does MCU still have a future?

29
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:05,890
MCU...

30
00:01:05,890 --> 00:01:10,860
For MCU, you definitely need to move on from just messing around like I mentioned earlier. You've got to develop in those kinds of industries.

31
00:01:10,860 --> 00:01:13,780
The automotive industry is definitely one of them.

32
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:18,850
I mean, I can't just say you can do it like before, you know, with nothing to show for it.

33
00:01:18,850 --> 00:01:20,490
You definitely need to be compliant with industry standards.

34
00:01:20,490 --> 00:01:24,260
Yeah, and it's developing in a way that's very industry-specific.

35
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:26,080
If you really just want to stick with MCU development,

36
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:28,800
And what do you mean by 'industry standards'?

37
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:31,640
Take the automotive industry for example, with its Functional safety standards.

38
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:32,959
The kind that are really strict in their standards.

39
00:01:32,959 --> 00:01:37,400
It's not the kind of thing where you can just hire anyone off the street and expect them to get started, you know?

40
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:39,760
So, for example, their coding standards,

41
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:40,520
or testing standards,

42
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:43,780
And the development processes are also very rigorous. Right.

43
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:49,280
So, what that means is, all these processes are a plus when it comes to getting a job.

44
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:55,370
Right. Yeah, so if you're applying for a job in the automotive industry, you might be able to get in.

45
00:01:55,370 --> 00:01:57,940
They're looking for those elite candidates with 1-3 years of experience.

46
00:01:57,940 --> 00:01:58,860
You might still have a shot at getting in.

47
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:01,300
But for those 5-10 year roles? You're pretty much not getting in, yeah.

48
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:02,680
Uh, so what do you think? Your classmate is asking you...

49
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:04,320
So, do you think you have the Curse of 35?

50
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:07,330
How much longer can I keep this up?

51
00:02:08,010 --> 00:02:09,250
Well, anyway, just try not to worry about it too much.

52
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:10,450
If you love what you do, that's all that matters.

53
00:02:10,450 --> 00:02:11,490
Don't even worry about that kind of crisis.

54
00:02:11,490 --> 00:02:14,690
Anyway, when the time comes, what will be, will be.

55
00:02:14,690 --> 00:02:16,550
I'm the kind of person who just rolls with the punches.

56
00:02:16,550 --> 00:02:17,430
So, in your company, you have positions...

57
